# Input graph for RDFLib__rdflib-leveldb__test_test_functionality.py__testSimpleGraph — written during translation.
#
# testSimpleGraph builds ALL of its own data (via .add()/+{ }) inside the two
# named graphs it opens through get_context(<urn:graph>) and
# get_context(<urn:othergraph>) — it never reads pre-existing content there.
# What this fixture exercises is that get_context() correctly ISOLATES named
# graphs: it seeds unrelated data in the DEFAULT graph (distinct from both
# <urn:graph> and <urn:othergraph>) that must not leak into either -- if it
# did, the region's own strict counts (assert len(g) == 3, len(g2) == 1, the
# "two people like pizza" / "tarek doesn't like cheese" query and pattern
# assertions) would fail identically on both sides, so the several-solutions,
# zero-solution and non-matching-neighbour cases the study asks for are
# already exercised by the region's own body against a graph seeded exactly
# this way. <urn:graph> and <urn:othergraph> are left empty here on purpose.
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .

ex:someone ex:likes ex:coffee .
